{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/950668-ideas-for-alternative-free-council-order-merit-needed","id":950668,"title":"Ideas for alternative Free Council Order merit needed","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-14T11:43:33-07:00","id":950668,"title":"Ideas for alternative Free Council Order merit needed","content":"So, I don't like Techne. Because of that, I would like some kind of replacement for it. Anyone got any ideas? I would love something based about Lorehouse, in similar manner to Egregore (to the point where I'm meditating upon just making a mirror merit for FC)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T12:10:13-07:00","id":950682,"title":"","content":"It's a bit out there, but you could adapt the Merit from the Vampire Dark Era that models alliances with supernatural societies. It could apply to Fallen magicians and skilled Sleepers affiliated with the Order.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T12:11:13-07:00","id":950683,"title":"","content":"What exactly don't you like about it? The concept? the mechanics? Both? It helps when making suggestions to know what the issue is.<br /> <br /> The problem with lorehouses being the focus is that they're not that integral to the FC. The Mysterium is dedicated to their Athenaeums (I don't know the correct plural and I suspect I misspelled it), it's the entire point. The concept of the assembly seems much more central to the FC.<br /> <br /> I dunno... channeling an egregore made from The People of an asembly could be interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T12:37:05-07:00","id":950688,"title":"","content":"Perhaps a merit that cancels the penalty to nonmagical actions when using mage sight to go with their magic in mundane everyday stuff thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","name":"Custos Tenebrarum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T12:45:24-07:00","id":950694,"title":"","content":"From what I understand of your perspective on the Free Council, I don't think we're likely to be able to develop a Merit that will both be appropriate to the Free Council as-written and be satisfying to you. I think that to fix Techne, we must first fix the Free Council. Once we've got a better idea of what a Free Council that suits your tastes looks like, then we can develop a Merit for it that stems from its themes and works within your game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T13:14:01-07:00","id":950714,"title":"","content":"I can think of a Merit that would give all members of the Free Council a positive impression of each other even if they should hate each other's guts, on the basis that they're all working towards a democratic consensus even if they disagree on certain points. <br /> <br /> No clue what it would do for spellcasting though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T16:58:04-07:00","id":950796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/950668-ideas-for-alternative-free-council-order-merit-needed?p=950683#post950683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What exactly don't you like about it? The concept? the mechanics? Both? It helps when making suggestions to know what the issue is.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the concept, I think that emphasizing the free council's focus on human culture is great. The problem for me is that it's too weak. A +1 Yantra is basically worthless, since they're so ubiquitous. If you have enough time to use computer programming as a Yantra, you could've found any number of other Yantras much more easily. Heck, you arguably could've just used computer programming as a Yantra anyway, even without the merit! That's not worth the exp cost at all.<br /> <br /> Then the fact that you need multiple characters to have the same 2-dot merit, just to get 8-again on teamwork spellcasting is way too much. Sure, it's nice, but you could also get that from a 2-dot Prime spell. Even worse is the fact that ALL characters participating in the teamwork spell must have Techne in order to give the bonus. Not only that, but they all must have the exact specific variety of Techne that you have. Consider the implications of that. If your cabalmates aren't Free Council, then they can't help you without ruining the Techne bonus. But there's a good chance that your cabalmates are strong enough that their contribution could easily offset the Techne bonus. In which case, Techne is giving you no benefit. Then, even if your cabalmates ARE Free Council, they probably aren't using the same kind of Techne you are, in which case they still can't help you.<br /> <br /> In other words, Techne is useful in such an incredibly narrow sliver of situations, that I don't even think it's worth a merit at all. I think the concept of focusing on human culture is perfect for the Free Council, but the execution is far too weak, niche, and expensive to be practical.<br /> <br /> <b>A simple fix</b> would be that Techne comes for free when you buy 2 merit dots that somehow relate to the aspect of human culture you're studying. I'd like to see a more comprehensive fix though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","user":"Strill","date":". 08-14-2016, 08:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T17:05:45-07:00","id":950798,"title":"","content":"Good point about pointing out what I don't like about Techne. Well, basically, it gives you nothing that can't be emulated by either picking a proper Dedicated Tool, adapting a fitting Shadow Name, or just using appropiate yantras - with the only unique benefit being the Sleeper thing, which isn't something I can see every single Libertine - or forget that, a majority of them - actually wanting enough to put two Experiences into. Basically, I feel it's doesn't change your gameplay patterns and doesn't provide you with unique experience that cannot be achieved without it. Each of other special merits gives you options that can, potentially, come up every session and change your play style. Techne just...is. <br /> <br /> So, a wish list - note that not all of these must be checked at the same time:<br /> <br /> - Something that can be used at least once every two game sessions assuming &quot;standard&quot; games of Mage that respect character focus (so if we have a character whose character sheet yells &quot;PUT ME IN A CAGE WITH A DRAGON I WANT TO FEAST ON IT HEART&quot;, Storyteller will throw a fight or two every now and then)<br /> - Something that emphasizes one of their universal tenets - so it's fitting both when you are Libertine Revolutionare, and when you are Ancient Tradition Goat Sacrificer, and when you are Mag Scientist<br /> - Something that changes their gameplay patterns, offering or emphasizing options that help characterize the Assembly <br /> - Something that is worth putting Experience into it;<br /> - Something that is &quot;exciting&quot; to use - active things that need to be declared or &quot;activated&quot; are more interesting than passive bonuses that just float somewhere <br /> <br /> For the &quot;Egregore but Free Council&quot;, I would see something like this:<br /> <br /> First dot - unchanged. Collective magic sounds proper.<br /> Second dot - unchanged. Again, this emphasizes the importance of being THE GROUP<br /> Third dot - I really like this Egregore dot, so something similar to it but based around idea of Lorehouse or political pull would be really cool<br /> Fourth dot - Again, this fits unchanged. It sounds more like Techne than actual Techne, even.<br /> Fifth dot - No idea what to replace it with, to be honest. <br /> <br /> Actually, I think something like 4th dot of Egregore + extra frills to make it good enough standalone would probably be cool enough for me. <br /> <br /> Example of idea I would like:<br /> &quot;Pick a magical style rooted in Sleeper world. You gain a special yantra slot that can be only used to incorporate an instrument from that magical style in your magic. It provides a yantra bonus appropriate to it's nature - so a tool will give you +1 bonus, while a rare sacrament will give you a +2 bonus - and in addition, always counts as a Dedicated Tool&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T02:44:13-07:00","id":951003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/950668-ideas-for-alternative-free-council-order-merit-needed?p=950798#post950798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Example of idea I would like:<br /> &quot;Pick a magical style rooted in Sleeper world. You gain a special yantra slot that can be only used to incorporate an instrument from that magical style in your magic. It provides a yantra bonus appropriate to it's nature - so a tool will give you +1 bonus, while a rare sacrament will give you a +2 bonus - and in addition, always counts as a Dedicated Tool&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Making <b><i>Techne</i></b> a +2 Yantra bonus or even Dedicated Tool sounds fair and cool enough for Free Council to make it pickable. I agree with <b>WHW</b> arguments on mechanics, only I like setting idea for <i>Techne</i> itself. I just think it should be much more powerful to be good in use in play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T14:55:15-07:00","id":952050,"title":"","content":"I have also been looking for a new Merit for FC, but in my case, it would be in addition to Techne. This is because I am already using this version for my games:<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Techne (2)</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Requisite:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Awakened, Free Council Status 1+.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Choose an aspect of human culture. This can be anything like \u201cbaseball\u201d, \u201calternative grunge rock\u201d, \u201celectronic sports\u201d, \u201cchinese taoism\u201d, \u201ccontemporary sculpture\u201d, \u201cfaith healing\u201d, \u201c18th-century poetry\u201d, \u201cMMA wrestling\u201d or anything else. The mage obtains a free specialty related to it on one of their skills, 1 free dot of Contacts or Allies who are related to that field, and can use elements from that aspect of culture as tool Yantras. Members of that culture do not count as Sleeper witnesses when the culture is used as a Yantra if the spell doesn\u2019t risk Paradox already. Finally, when casting a spell as a Ritual, Sleepers from that culture can participate on the Ritual as if they were Sleepwalkers if the spell doesn\u2019t risk Paradox. This Merit may be purchased multiple times, once per cultural aspect desired.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2535-arthexis","name":"arthexis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T15:21:34-07:00","id":952075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/950668-ideas-for-alternative-free-council-order-merit-needed?p=950796#post950796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>A simple fix</b> would be that Techne comes for free when you buy 2 merit dots that somehow relate to the aspect of human culture you're studying. I'd like to see a more comprehensive fix though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could we do this backwards-ish? Maybe something that grows both from width (&quot;contact with <i>more cultures</i>&quot;) and from depth (&quot;contact with <i>more people involved in a culture</i>.&quot;) The goal would be to hit both the &quot;globetrotting modern coalitionist&quot; Council and the &quot;culture-invested traditionalist&quot; Council.<br /> <br /> Techne (1 or 2 dots?):<br /> Prereqs: Free Council Stat 1, Contacts 1<br /> <br /> For every set of mortal Contacts the character has:<br /> They may treat the functions and activities of that role as an Order Tool for the Free Council if they enact or invoke them during spellcasting.<br /> They may further treat the presence of Sleepers engaging in them as a separate Order tool, which does not count against their limit of harnessed yantras.<br /> If three(?) or more Sleepers are performing the task, the performance counts as a Dedicated Tool if harnessed.<br /> <br /> Alternatively (or in addition)<br /> <br /> Arete (1 or 2 dots?):<br /> Prereqs: Free Council Stat 1, Contacts 1<br /> <br /> For every set of mortal Contacts the character has:<br /> They may treat the functions and activities of that role as an Order Tool for the Free Council if they enact or invoke them during spellcasting.<br /> Once per chapter they may recover a single point of mana if they witness a Sleeper achieve an exceptional success in these functions, as if the mage had performed an oblation; the mage can perceive the flow of meaning between adept human action and supernal significance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":1653,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","user":"Five Eyes","date":".  Cleaned up some wording. 08-17-2016, 03:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T01:59:08-07:00","id":954279,"title":"","content":"Forewarning: I like to break the game for dramatic effect.<br /> <br /> That being said, my house rule for the Free Council merit is that when Libertines ACTIVELY engage Sleepers in their spell casting, they can get some pretty massive bonuses. When they use this merit, free &quot;reach&quot; is applied towards the primary spell factor (which includes potency in my games). The more effort that is put into grounding the spell in Sleeper society, the more the players are able to move up the chart in spell factors.<br /> <br /> An example from my current game - a FC cabal in Chicago:<br /> The cabal just claimed a very large territory of about four suburbs south of the city, and attention turned to security. They wanted to set up a perimeter where any Supernal magic done within its limits pings on their radar. The area required would put this in the range of mastery or arch-mastery. However, the cabal spent nearly 4 months of in-game time (and about 4 gaming sessions) setting up a community watch program in these neighborhoods. They spent a massive amount of time withdrawn from Mage society and building the Sleeper institution into the imago of this massive spell. The night their neighborhood watch caught its first petty thief home invader, the imago of protection and defense was complete and they were able to release a spell with enough free juice to completely max out the AoE spell factors- for free! They spent the rest of their reach (obtained normally) on other effects.<br /> <br /> Is this incredibly broken-- yes! Is it incredibly fun -- hell yes! I and all of my players have a huge soft spot for the Free Council, so anything to drive home the message that humanity is magical and the FC as guardians and shepherds of humanities magical potential is permissible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5202,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5202-hotchepsoot","user":"HotChepSoot","date":". 08-20-2016, 05:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5202-hotchepsoot","name":"HotChepSoot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5202_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T02:13:57-07:00","id":954282,"title":"","content":"I rewrote all the order merits as 1 to 5 dot progressions when they were spoiled. This is what I came up with for Techne, hopefully it helps.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><u>Techne \u2022 - \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</u></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><b>Prerequisites</b>: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">Techne reflects a personal investment in a sleeper tradition, therefore a character can qualify for it with any merit that represents his connection to that group: Contacts \u2022, Mystery Cult Initiation \u2022, Allies \u2022, Status \u2022, etc.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><b>Effect</b>: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">Your character uses Libertine practices in order to use cultural magical styles, sciences, and art forms as magical tools.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><b>Area of Interest</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">(\u2022): You may treat the presence of Sleepers employing the yantra of your spell as a separate Yantra, with a bonus based on the number of sleepers involved (+1 for a few to +3 for a large group), as long as the spell is not obvious.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><b>Group Project</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">(\u2022\u2022): Sleeper assistants apply their Paradox modifier as a bonus to the spell. A small group provides 9 again, a crowd 8-again, and a significant congregation grants the Rote quality. Again, only if the spell is not obvious.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><b>Think Tank</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">(\u2022\u2022\u2022): The Yantra bonus provided by Sleepers now counts as an additional dedicated tool, reducing Paradox by two.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><b>Interdisciplinary Studies</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">(\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022): Multiple Libertines with this merit may add their sleeper congregation's relevant Yantra bonus to their own teamwork bonus, even if the spell being cast wouldn't normally resonate with their Yantra.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">Gestalt </span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\">(\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022): Sleepers participating in your ritual are considered sleepwalkers with regards to all spells they help you cast. The limit on non-obvious spells is also removed.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}